	(text "A11b (25.10.2026, owner list M3): the LS07 drivers U6/U7 are replaced by six dual N-MOSFETs Q6-Q11 (Diodes BSS138DW-7-F, VGS(th) <= 1.5 V, RDS(on) <= 3.5 Ohm at 10 V): gate = MCU line FDD_*, drain = bus line FD_* (open drain, pulled up by the 1k terminations on FDD_5V), source = GND; R144-R155 100k gate pull-downs keep every line released through reset. An LS07 guarantees 0.4 V only up to 16 mA, the drive's 150 Ohm terminator alone draws 33 mA.\nPolarity: MCU high = bus low (the LS07 was non-inverting), the firmware flips bus_out()/TIM3_CH1/TIM15_CH1 on board_rev >= 10 (board.h board_fdd_mosfet). IEC driver U9 stays an LS07 (three 1k pull-ups = 15 mA, within its spec). Channels: Q6 MOTOR_A/MOTOR_B, Q7 DRVSEL_A/DRVSEL_B, Q8 STEP/DIR, Q9 SIDE/WGATE_G, Q10 WDATA/DENSITY, Q11 DRATE/INDEX_SIM (onto the INDEX bus)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 230 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "26ba033a-4e09-4f94-b1d3-d0e3c848e62a")
	)
